    "created_at": "2016-05-10T19:09:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-10T19:13:36Z",
    "body": "This is handled by Web IDL. Those parameters are declared `optional long timeout`, so they are converted to Web IDL long types (which can be compared to numbers) before the algorithm ever runs.\n\n(If you are interested in the exact algorithm for converting any JavaScript value to a Web IDL long type, see https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#es-long)\n\nI have no idea why the W3C fork does anything that it does. Nobody implements it, so I wouldn't bother paying attention to it.\n\nClosing since I believe this is is solved, but happy to continue discussion, and will reopen if I missed something.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
